{"actor_identity":"/root/anonymous_decoder58","assumptions":"Only the supplied measurable-space structures and MeasurePreserving f μ ν: f is measurable and its pushforward of μ is ν. No finite-measure, probability, standard-Borel, countable-generation or invertibility hypothesis appears.","conclusion":"range(C_f)=lpMeas(ℝ,ℝ,f⁻¹Σ_Y,2,μ), as actual real linear submodules of L²(X,μ;ℝ).","confidence":0.99,"constant_dependencies":"Scalar field and function values are ℝ and exponent is exactly 2. No numerical bound or variable constant occurs; the range submodule depends on f,Σ_Y,μ and pullback depends also on ν through measure preservation.","decoder":"/root/anonymous_decoder58","decoder_packet_sha256":"7cdd56aa4942dd72f8ee32c365af1f293ce418a1d6ffa5de52c2c1b8effd297c","decoder_run_id":"anonymous_decoder58","domains":"Arbitrary types X,Y with measurable spaces. μ∈Measure(X), ν∈Measure(Y), f:X→Y. Domain of C_f is L²(Y,ν;ℝ); codomain and both sides of the range equality lie in real L²(X,μ). Measures may be infinite.","input_artifact":{"canonical_decoder_packet_sha256":"7cdd56aa4942dd72f8ee32c365af1f293ce418a1d6ffa5de52c2c1b8effd297c","lf_bytes":2169,"lf_sha256":"d93fd47d9fdddcb9d01f1c41fd611b46d043f6cca010254e8d0e32c1baae0d78","path":"packet0.json","raw_bytes":2216,"raw_sha256":"e88260e6fa4f70a29b443b28ea7c9fdcf971d83db0daf86d8bccce224bb316bd"},"objects":"X,Y; their measurable structures Σ_X,Σ_Y; measures μ,ν; f; real L² equivalence-class spaces; canonical composition linear isometry C_f; the submodule lpMeas for f⁻¹Σ_Y.","packet_id":"ASTIS-BLIND-def943130bc1749a","quantifiers":"Universally over X,Y, their measurable structures, μ,ν, and f, subject to measure preservation. The submodule equality means every pullback class lies in lpMeas and every class in lpMeas is the pullback of some marginal L² class.","reconstructed_text_sha256":"102ff839a06adb91e3738e3b580881d8fbb1190d2bc6b00565da79adad07ca2b","reconstructed_theorem":"Let X and Y be arbitrary measurable spaces, let μ and ν be measures on them, and let f:X→Y be measure preserving (measurable with f_*μ=ν). Canonical pullback g↦g∘f is a real linear isometry from L²(Y,ν;ℝ) to L²(X,μ;ℝ). Its image is exactly the real linear subspace of L²(X,μ;ℝ) consisting of classes that admit μ-almost-everywhere strongly measurable representatives for the pullback σ-algebra f⁻¹Σ_Y. No finiteness or probability assumption is imposed on either measure.","reconstructed_theorem_text":"Let X and Y be arbitrary measurable spaces, let μ and ν be measures on them, and let f:X→Y be measure preserving (measurable with f_*μ=ν). Canonical pullback g↦g∘f is a real linear isometry from L²(Y,ν;ℝ) to L²(X,μ;ℝ). Its image is exactly the real linear subspace of L²(X,μ;ℝ) consisting of classes that admit μ-almost-everywhere strongly measurable representatives for the pullback σ-algebra f⁻¹Σ_Y. No finiteness or probability assumption is imposed on either measure.","schema_version":1,"scopes":"Equality of submodules of almost-everywhere equivalence classes, not pointwise equality of all function representatives. lpMeas uses almost-everywhere strong measurability for the comap measurable structure. No conditional-expectation, centeredness or probability conclusion is stated.","semantic_slots":{"assumptions":"Only the supplied measurable-space structures and MeasurePreserving f μ ν: f is measurable and its pushforward of μ is ν. No finite-measure, probability, standard-Borel, countable-generation or invertibility hypothesis appears.","conclusion":"range(C_f)=lpMeas(ℝ,ℝ,f⁻¹Σ_Y,2,μ), as actual real linear submodules of L²(X,μ;ℝ).","constant_dependencies":"Scalar field and function values are ℝ and exponent is exactly 2. No numerical bound or variable constant occurs; the range submodule depends on f,Σ_Y,μ and pullback depends also on ν through measure preservation.","domains":"Arbitrary types X,Y with measurable spaces. μ∈Measure(X), ν∈Measure(Y), f:X→Y. Domain of C_f is L²(Y,ν;ℝ); codomain and both sides of the range equality lie in real L²(X,μ). Measures may be infinite.","objects":"X,Y; their measurable structures Σ_X,Σ_Y; measures μ,ν; f; real L² equivalence-class spaces; canonical composition linear isometry C_f; the submodule lpMeas for f⁻¹Σ_Y.","quantifiers":"Universally over X,Y, their measurable structures, μ,ν, and f, subject to measure preservation. The submodule equality means every pullback class lies in lpMeas and every class in lpMeas is the pullback of some marginal L² class.","scopes":"Equality of submodules of almost-everywhere equivalence classes, not pointwise equality of all function representatives. lpMeas uses almost-everywhere strong measurability for the comap measurable structure. No conditional-expectation, centeredness or probability conclusion is stated."},"source_identity_visible":false,"source_text_visible":false,"unresolved_ambiguities":[]}
